WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.850
Evening.

2
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.060
A family watches the
news on Channel Example.

3
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:07.600
The newsreader says
bath with a long vowel.

4
00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:11.530
Their son scrolls videos from all
over the country on his phone.

5
00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:15.410
Next morning at the bus stop, he
tells his mates he needs a bath.

6
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:16.650
Short vowel.

7
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.620
Decades of national broadcasting,
and now the internet.

8
00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:23.500
So why are regional accents still here?

9
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:26.220
In this mission, you'll pull apart accent,

10
00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:30.300
which is sounds, and dialect,
which is words and grammar.

11
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:33.150
You'll see how an accent can carry status,

12
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.900
and ask what else it quietly signals.

13
00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.970
And you'll track accents
that are still changing,

14
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.620
and ask who speakers are moving towards.

15
00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:45.500
Your mission: explain
why accents survive TV,

16
00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:47.230
radio and the internet.
